[color=#f1c232][b]
[size=6]HORSIE GO WHERE HORSIE LOOK*.
RDR2 style "horse relative" mount controls.[/size][/b][/color]
[size=2][i]* and Wagon, Ibex, Camel, Snow Deer, Boar, Bear, Wolf, Tiger, Lion, Iguana, Raptor, Kuku Bird (steering works while gliding too), elephant[/i][/size]


[size=4]I do not like horse being tied to the camera. I wanna look around while riding.[/size]
[size=4]"Horse Relative" means the direction the horse travels is disconnected from the camera. Think of it like riding an actual horse (I have never ridden a horse IRL but this feels like a good way to describe it).[/size]



[color=#f1c232][size=4][b]What do?[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*]Horsie go where horsie look! You look but horsie not care. Horsie go where horsie look. (why am I writing like this?)[/*]
[*]Change where horsie look with A and D (or stick). So easy.[/*]
[*]Change horsie speed with tap on S / brake / back on stick, hold to slow down all the way.[/*]
[*]Horsie can reverse now. Like... walk backwards. Waow.[/*]
[*]Wagon go where horsie look![/*]
[*]Wagon reverse with S key (or down on stick). Still reverse with normal button too.[/*]
[*]No change taming minigame (even though I could have left it and then with this mod you'd have been able to instantly win by holding one button).[/*]
[/list]

[b]*Note:[/b] Get tighter turns on horsie by letting go of W.

[color=#f1c232][size=4][b]Controls:[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*]Proper horse controls[/*]
[*][b]F5[/b] - Toggle the mod on/off.[/*]
[*]Reversing turns the wrong way for brain? Set [b]InvertSteer=0[/b] in the ini.[/*]
[/list]
[size=2][i]Technically controller should be supported but I cannot test this. If it works on controller, cool! Otherwise, feedback wanted.[/i][/size]



[color=#f1c232][size=4][b]Settings:[/b][/size][/color]
[spoiler]
[i]This is all documented inside the [b].ini[/b], but I know some folks want to know everything possible about a mod before they choose to try it out. Press [b]End[/b] in game after editing your [b].ini[/b] file to reload. Only Logging still needs a game restart.
[/i]

[b][color=#f1c232][Features] CameraDetached[/color][/b]
The whole point of the mod. Default 1. Set 0 and horsie go where camera look again, like base game. Also turns off walking backwards, wagon S reverse and back on stick to slow down.

[b][color=#f1c232][Features] TapBrake[/color][/b]
Tap S, brake or back on stick to slow down. Default 1, set 0 to turn it off. If CameraDetached is off, tap S (with W held) and brake still work, but back on stick is just the game's normal go that way.

[b][color=#f1c232][Steering] KeyRampMs[/color][/b]
How long A and D take to steer all the way, 0 to 500 ms. Default 300. Horsie too slow to turn and you keep hitting trees? Go lower. 0 is full steer instantly. Controller not affected, stick already smooth.

[b][color=#f1c232][Steering] LowSpeed, LowSpeedBias, HighSpeed, HighSpeedBias[/color][/b]
How hard W+A/D turns horsie. Bias 0 is straight ahead, 1 is straight sideways, but it tops out at 0.94 so horsie still goes somewhere. LowSpeedBias is used at LowSpeed m/s and below, HighSpeedBias at HighSpeed and above, and it blends in between. Defaults 2.2, 0.89, 4.8, 0.61. Want to carve tighter at a gallop? Raise HighSpeedBias. Works on controller too.

[b][color=#f1c232][Keys] Toggle[/color][/b]
Key to turn the mod on/off. Default F5. F1-F24, A-Z, 0-9, Numpad0-Numpad9, Insert, Delete, Home, End, PageUp, PageDown, Pause or ScrollLock. Not W, A, S or D.

[b][color=#f1c232][Keys] Reload[/color][/b]
Key to reload your [b].ini[/b] while playing. Default End. Takes the same keys as Toggle. Make it the same key as Toggle and that key does both, so maybe don't.

[b][color=#f1c232][Reverse] InvertSteer[/color][/b]
Which way A and D turn horsie when reversing. Default 1, set 0 to flip it. Works on wagon too.

[b][color=#f1c232][Reverse] StickDeadzone[/color][/b]
How far you can lean the stick sideways and it still counts as straight back, 0 to 1. Default 0.30. 0 is no leeway, 0.5 is a 45 degree lean, 1 ignores left and right while pulling back. Horsie spin when you wanted reverse? Need more bigger deadzone.

[b][color=#f1c232][BackwardSpeed][/color][/b]
How fast each kind of mount walks backward, 0.2 to 6 m/s. Ibex uses the horse value, snow deer uses reindeer, tiger and lion use Wolf_Elite.

[b][color=#f1c232][Debug] Logging[/color][/b]
Default 0. Set 1 if you're reporting a bug and want to send me logs. About 10MB per hour of riding, and they get wiped every game start, so save them before relaunching.[/spoiler]



[color=#f1c232][size=4][b]Installation:[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/crimsondesert/mods/633]DMM[/url]:[/b] add the downloaded zip as a mod, enable it and apply.[/*]
[*][b]Manual:[/b] copy [b]ProperHorseControls.asi[/b] and [b]ProperHorseControls.ini[/b] from the [b]ProperHorseControls[/b] folder into the game's [b]bin64[/b] folder. Requires ASI loader.[/*]
[*]Uninstalling?: remove both files from [b]bin64[/b].[/*]
[/list]

[b][color=#f1c232][size=4]Known issues:[/size][/color][/b]
[list]
[*]Wagons still control poorly in reverse, just like base game. I ain't touching that.[/*]
[*]After winning the taming minigame, the horse controls can freeze if you choose to ride it immediately. Dismount and remount to fix it[/*]
[*]Should keep working with game updates, but if not, patch will come soon. Please wait :)[/*]
[/list]

[b][color=#f1c232][size=4]Compatibility:[/size][/color][/b]
[list]
[*]Any mod that changes mount or riding inputs will probably conflict[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/crimsondesert/mods/3175]Crimson Route[/url] - ✅[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/crimsondesert/mods/3666]Horse Tap Brake[/url] - not compatible. I done eated their mod to help make mine better (with permission). [/*]
[/list]

[b][color=#f1c232][size=4]For mod authors:[/size][/color][/b]
[spoiler]If your mod drives the mount by itself, like auto run, you can suspend ProperHorseControls using the snippet below. It is safe to call even if ProperHorseControls is not installed. Function is threadsafe and idempotent.

[code]
// suspended: 1 = true, 0 = false.
// If you never send 0 after suspending PHC, it remains suspended until the game is closed.
// Don't call this at startup. ASI load order isn't guaranteed, so PHC may not be loaded yet and the lookup will fail.
void SetPhcSuspended(int32_t suspended) {
    using SetSuspended = void (*)(const char* owner, int32_t suspended);
    if (HMODULE phc = GetModuleHandleW(L"ProperHorseControls.asi")) {
        if (auto set = reinterpret_cast<SetSuspended>(GetProcAddress(phc, "PHC_SetSuspended"))) {
            // Replace YourModName with your mod's name. Names are truncated to 31 characters.
            // If several mods suspend PHC, it stays suspended until all of them have sent 0.
            // It tracks up to 16 mods and ignores any more.
            set("YourModName", suspended);
        }
    }
}[/code][/spoiler]

[b][color=#f1c232][size=4]AI Disclosure:[/size][/color][/b]
[spoiler]The code for this mod was written with Claude (Anthropic's AI).

The design, documentation, reference material, testing approach, and silly sounding mod description was created by me.

Zero functions of any other person's work were cloned, stolen, or directly replicated to make this mod. The one feature idea I borrowed is tap to slow down from Horse Tap Brake, with its author's permission, and it's built differently here (see Credits).[/spoiler]



